{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he offered and they sacrificed.</b> For the joy of the goodness that HaKadosh Barukh Hu did for Israel." "<b>And Aaron came and all the elders of Israel.</b> But Moses did not need to come, for the tent was his, and they all came there in honor of Jethro his father-in-law." "<b>Before the Elohim.</b> According to the plain sense, לפני means 'before,' like מלפני — that is, from what they offered before HaKadosh Barukh Hu, and they are the peace-offerings."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:32.032433493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}